Auto Commands - vim in event driven
autocmd will create callbacks/hooks (another event) when specified 	
	events are triggered


syntax 
 :autocmd <EventType> <pattern> <command>

many buffer related auto commands

:h autocmd-events
Event Types: 
	- Buffer 
	- File
	...
	- Interactions (lost focus)

autocmd BufNewFile *.h 0r ~/template/skeleton.h
	EventType: BufNewFile
	Pattern: *.h
	collon command: 0r ~/template/skeleton.h
		'go to line 0 and read from file'

autcmd BufNewFile *.p[lm] call BuildFileTemplate(<afile>)
	
autocdm BufReadPost *.[ch] %!indent -st
	" after reading information into a buffer run the indent command on the
	" whole buffer
autocdm FileReadPost *.[ch] %!indent -st
	" after reading into a file ...	

autocmd BufRead *.[ch] set cindent
autocmd FileRead *.[ch] set cindent
		

